{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovParameterRecursion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovParameterRecursion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovParamCoeff_recursion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovParamCoeff_recursion","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovParameterRecursion.lean#L84-L99","doc":"**The defining recursion**, in the index-shifted form used by the\ndefinition: for every `n`,\n\n  `4(n+2)·a_{n+2} + 6(n+1)·a_{n+1} + (2n+1)·a_n = 0`.\n\nThis is the holonomic / q-difference recursion the Markov-parameter\ncoefficients satisfy — the categorical object whose archimedean\nevaluation at `q₀` feeds the Q_β precision ladder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovParamCoeff_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovParamCoeff_four","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovParameterRecursion.lean#L80-L82","doc":"`a₄ = −13/256`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovParamCoeff_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovParamCoeff_three","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovParameterRecursion.lean#L76-L78","doc":"`a₃ = 1/16`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovParamCoeff_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovParamCoeff_two","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovParameterRecursion.lean#L71-L74","doc":"`a₂ = −1/16` — first nontrivial coefficient, matching the\nsymbolic series of `√q/(1+q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovParamCoeff_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovParamCoeff_one","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovParameterRecursion.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovParamCoeff_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovParamCoeff_zero","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovParameterRecursion.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovParamCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovParamCoeff","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovParameterRecursion.lean#L51-L65","doc":"Taylor coefficients `aₙ` of the Markov parameter `z(q) = √q/(1+q)`\nexpanded around `q = 1` (`w = q − 1`), defined by the holonomic\nrecursion derived from `(4 + 6w + 2w²) z' + w z = 0`:\n\n  `a₀ = 1/2`, `a₁ = 0`,\n  `4(n+2)·a_{n+2} = −(6(n+1)·a_{n+1} + (2n+1)·a_n)`.\n\nPre-archimedean: every value is an exact rational. ","signatureChunk":0}]}